WEBVTT

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.950
<i>In the year 2020 C.E.,</i>

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>the human world is connected by a network.</i>

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:24.160
<i>Inhabiting it is
an unknown life form called Digimon.</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.310
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.310
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.770
<i>The mysterious Digimon that infests
the Network continues to evolve.</i>

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:16.990
<i>It transforms into a menacing figure
and overpowers Taichi and the others.</i>

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.910
<i>It goes on a rampage and
the missile closes in on Tokyo.</i>

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.740
<i>That very moment...</i>

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.200
Taichi.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.710
Yamato.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:14.880
Now,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.590
let's go!

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.390
AND TO THE DIGITAL WORLD

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.440
Is this... a Digimon too?

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.630
<i>Taichi-san! Yamato-san!</i>

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.430
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:50.720
Koshiro?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.350
<i>Can you see the missile's trajectory?</i>

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.390
<i>It's almost going to hit!</i>

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.900
It looks like
there's a black box in the system.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.730
We won't be able to stop the explosion!

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:05.650
<i>"Someone stop it!"</i>

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.290
There's no choice,
let's blow the missile up!

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.460
We have to do it ourselves!

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.470
We can do it now...

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.500
Go.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.750
What's that?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.760
Huh?!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.640
It stopped working!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.640
I wanted a picture...

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.900
No way! This is bad.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.640
Oh, it turned back on.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.190
I thought it broke!

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.400
What was that?

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.400
Is something wrong?

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:35.940
Uh-uh.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.110
It's nothing.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.380
Hello, Mom? Are you okay?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.380
Uh, yeah.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.550
I see.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.720
Yeah, take care. See you later.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.300
Phew.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.680
How was your family?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.930
Oh, they were fine.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.140
Gee, I'm glad you picked up my phone!

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:12.270
Taichi-san, how on earth
were you able to return to this world?

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.650
Ermm...

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.900
We blew the missile up,

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:19.110
then a bright light came over us.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.820
And I was on the station platform
before I knew it.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.410
Tell me how this side was that moment.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.620
Yes.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:31.000
After the missile was knocked off
its trajectory by all of you...

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.290
it exploded far above Tokyo in the sky.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:39.170
At the same time, all electronic devices
stopped working for a moment.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:43.800
I think a phenomenon
like an electromagnetic pulse occurred.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:48.140
When an enormous explosion
occurs in an extremely high place,

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.440
devices and data in an area
are damaged as a result.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:56.020
Normally, they would all break completely,

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.610
but the damages were momentary.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:03.280
I wonder if a mysterious power intervened.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.910
Hmm.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:09.160
But... maybe the reason why
you were able to return

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.620
is because this world
and the world of the Network

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.750
were cut off due to the phenomenon.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.880
Hmm...

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:21.630
By the way, that giant, white Digimon...

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.880
I wonder what that was.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.350
Ermm...

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.720
Everything's a mystery...

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:35.480
Well, at least everyone's safe,
so let's leave it at that.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.190
That's true!

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:43.360
Agumon and them weren't a dream, right?

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.570
Everything that happened this morning

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.700
is very clear in my memory.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.710
Right.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:56.250
Since you came over
and we ran out after seeing the news,

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:59.420
it hasn't even been an hour yet, huh?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.010
I'm sure they're all fine.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:05.300
Agumon, Garurumon, and Yamato-san too.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.390
Yeah.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.470
Yamato...

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:12.730
He probably went back
to where he's from too.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:13.640
Oh...

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:17.600
In the end, I forgot
to ask him where he lives!

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.400
Oh! You're right...

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:25.280
What happened today is just between us.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.410
Yes.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:31.540
Well, no one would believe us
even if we did tell.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:32.620
Hm?

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.250
Thanks, Koshiro.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.710
Huh? I didn't do anything.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:41.670
You looked everything up and informed us.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:43.380
And supported us.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:45.550
You really saved us all.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.430
You're seriously awesome, Koshiro.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.470
Thank you!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:56.060
I'm glad I was able to help too!

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:04.650
If we get another chance,
let's go to that world together!

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:05.940
Okay!

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.160
Huh?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.030
By the way...

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.910
Koshiro, didn't you come over to talk
about the camping trip?

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:16.910
Oh!

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.260
We're home!

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.760
Phew, what a hectic day!

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.430
I got a call earlier,

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:32.470
but your dad's place
was full of trouble too.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.600
Now, gotta prepare dinner...

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.180
Oh, Hikari.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:40.350
This morning was a disaster!
Were you scared?

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.730
Yeah, a little.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.270
You did good!

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.650
Taichi... thank you.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:48.740
Huh?

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.660
Oh, Taichi!

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.870
Did you finish preparing for camp?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.910
That's right...

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.670
<i>Were you okay there?</i>

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.130
Um, yeah.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:05.500
I was home all day today, so I'm fine.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.760
<i>I see, that's good.</i>

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.130
You seem well.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.640
<i>Yeah, I'm good!</i>

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:17.640
<i>Hey, it's summer break,
so can we see each other?</i>

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.140
Yeah, I'll come visit next time...

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.690
To Tokyo.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.450
You kids!

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:35.410
You aren't cutting the vegetables right!
Leave this to the group leader here!

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.660
Time sure flies.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:41.790
No one's even talking
about that incident anymore.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:42.920
Seems like it.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.960
Well, that's how it is.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.750
About that missile...

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.010
"It was launched in error by the U.S.,

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:52.340
and shot down
by their own defense missiles."

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.800
At least, that's the story online.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:59.220
But we're the ones who blew that thing up.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.140
So messed up.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:06.320
That's why it's fun to search
for the real story behind the news.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.070
You really are awesome.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.950
My finger! I cut my finger!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.910
Call an ambulance!

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:15.070
Whoa!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.280
Hup.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:18.910
There.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.170
Sora, perfect timing.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.170
Here!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.210
Thank you so much!

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:28.210
Um...

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.590
You're Sora Takenouchi-san, right?

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.470
Yeah, you know me?

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:35.510
Yes.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.720
Even in my class,

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:41.180
all the girls talk about you,
saying that you're really cool.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.690
I'll introduce you. He's a fourth-grader.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.730
I'm Koshiro Izumi.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.980
Nice to meet you, Koshiro-kun.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:50.820
Takenouchi-san!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.150
Oh. Coming!

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.570
Then I'll see you.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:55.740
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:59.330
Sora-san is in the same class as you,
right Taichi-san?

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:03.750
Yeah, we go back a long way
before that though.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:12.340
After that incident,
I've been thinking about what Digimon are.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:16.090
One theory is that
when artificial intelligence develops,

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.760
it evolves into a life form.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:22.600
You mean Agumon and them
are A.I. or something?

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:24.270
I'm not sure.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:27.150
It doesn't really make sense, does it?

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:30.480
Besides, there's still
another question remaining.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:33.780
Why did the missile target Tokyo?

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:38.070
There's no theories even online.
Everyone's practically given up.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:39.950
Well, yeah.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.160
Maybe they wanted to blow us up

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.290
along with the city
because we got in their way?

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:47.880
That is a possibility.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.920
If so, what was their original goal?

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:58.510
I have a feeling an incident
like that will occur again.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:01.680
An unresolved mystery and Digimon.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:05.640
I'm sure we haven't seen the last
of whatever we came across before.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:09.650
Yeah, it doesn't feel like it's over yet.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:49.100
<i>Power outages have occurred</i>

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:52.900
<i>and are still spreading
in several areas in the city.</i>

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:57.240
<i>After investigation, its origin was found
to be a power supply network error.</i>

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:01.030
<i>Power companies are working
to find the cause of this error,</i>

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.780
<i>but there are no signs
of recovery as of yet.</i>

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:07.410
<i>There are growing concerns
that utilities will be affected.</i>

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.920
<i>The government has suggested...</i>

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.130
Electronics going haywire before,

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.040
<i>"Now a power outage..."</i>

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.670
and now a power outage...

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.380
<i>"I'm outside right now."</i>

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.880
<i>"Seems like our area isn't affected."</i>

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:24.680
<i>"And the internet's still working."</i>

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:24.680
Oh yeah, I still have a connection...

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:27.640
<i>"Trains are off-schedule."</i>

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:29.390
According to the last case
and the current one,

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:33.150
I simulated
what would happen going forward.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:37.990
<i>If this power outage continues to grow...</i>

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:45.160
<i>in approximately 72 hours,
the city will completely stop functioning.</i>

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.870
<i>In other words, a blackout will occur.</i>

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.620
<i>The town we live in
is no exception either...</i>

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.170
<i>Um, Taichi-san!</i>

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.170
Yours too?

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.300
<i>It's lighting up!</i>

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:01.680
<i>But it's been quiet since that time...</i>

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:03.090
Where are you now?

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.640
<i>The bench in front of the station!</i>

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.010
I'll be right there!

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.270
Taichi?

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.560
Are you going out?

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.110
Hikari, make sure to stay
inside the house.

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:17.650
With Mom.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.690
Got that?

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:19.900
Okay.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.280
Bye-bye.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.830
<i>Is it you?</i>

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.040
<i>Are you calling... for me?</i>

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.720
<i>We're the only ones...</i>

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.060
<i>who can stop this, right?</i>

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.350
<i>Let's do it once more...</i>

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:56.860
Agumon!

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:22.550
It's different...

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.630
from before?

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:29.560
Taichi.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.860
Agumon...

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:56.580
This is us Digimon's home...

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:00.630
the Digital World.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:07.380
<i>As if rolling out of control,
I ran frantically</i>

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:07.380
<i>korogaru youni gamushara ni hashitta</i>

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.260
<i>"What's waiting ahead?"</i>

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.260
<i>nani ga matteru no?</i>

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:17.770
<i>The headwinds told me</i>

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:17.770
<i>mukaikaze ga oshiete kuretanda</i>

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>"Just believe and move forward"</i>

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>shinjite susume</i>

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.490
<i>The bitter taste of defeat is a seed</i>

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.490
<i>yaburete shitta kuyashisa wa tane</i>

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.110
<i>It will eventually sprout
And become your wings</i>

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.110
<i>yagate mebuki hane to naru</i>

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.950
<i>I knock on those doors</i>

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.950
<i>sono tobira tataku riyuu</i>

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:36.790
<i>Because the present shapes the future</i>

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:36.790
<i>ima ga mirai wo tsukuru kara</i>

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.080
<i>If you want to find a rainbow</i>

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.080
<i>niji wo mitsuketai nara</i>

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>You must lift your face</i>

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>kao wo agenakuchatte</i>

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:47.510
<i>The hands that reached out to us
Make us much stronger</i>

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:47.510
<i>sashidasareta te ga
bokura wo zutto tsuyoku suru</i>

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.590
<i>If you want to catch your dreams</i>

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.590
<i>yume wo tsukamitai nara</i>

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>Though the step forward is unsteady</i>

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>furueru sono ippo mae ni</i>

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.640
<i>Try and take it</i>

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.640
<i>fumi dashite goran yo</i>

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>Because you can surely fly now</i>

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>ima nara kitto sora mo toberu kara</i>

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:06.490
<i>With Taichi and the others in danger,
Sora's Digivice lights up!</i>

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:11.160
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"Birdramon Soars"</i>

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:14.030
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
